## 4. BLUR DESIGN PILLARS

The game must preserve the following gameplay pillars.

### Pillar 1 — Vehicle credibility

Vehicles must look and behave like believable high-performance automobiles.

Avoid cartoon karts, primitive cubes and toy-like vehicles.

### Pillar 2 — Accessible arcade handling

Driving must be easy to learn but difficult to master.

Cars must have distinguishable grip, weight, acceleration and drift behavior.

### Pillar 3 — Tactical combat

Power-ups must interact with each other.

Combat must reward timing, aiming, positioning and defensive decisions.

### Pillar 4 — Continuous progression

Every race must provide meaningful rewards for driving skill, combat, defensive actions and challenges.

### Pillar 5 — Competitive social racing

The game must eventually support large multiplayer races, competitive ranks, rivalries and player challenges.

### Pillar 6 — Readable high-speed action

Visual effects must communicate gameplay clearly without obscuring the road.

