## 10. VEHICLE HANDLING ARCHETYPES

Implement four distinct driving identities.

### Grippy

- Strong lateral grip.
- Stable cornering.
- Low tendency to oversteer.
- Easy recovery.
- Less aggressive drift behavior.

### Drifty

- Higher controllable lateral slip.
- Responsive weight transfer.
- Stronger oversteer tendency.
- Effective corner exit when mastered.
- Greater difficulty for inexperienced players.

### Balanced

- Moderate grip.
- Moderate drift capability.
- Predictable steering.
- Versatile track performance.

### Off-road

- Better traction on dirt and gravel.
- Improved stability on uneven terrain.
- Increased durability where appropriate.
- Different asphalt handling characteristics.

These archetypes must change actual simulation behavior.

Do not implement them only as labels in the garage.

